<title>UK: IGC lowers forecast for 1997 FSU cereals production.</title>
<headline>IGC lowers forecast for 1997 FSU cereals production.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Grains Council (IGC) on Thursday cut its forecast for grains production in the former Soviet Union by 4.1 million tonnes to 129.6 million, IGC data showed.</p>
<p>The forecast for coarse grains output fell by 2.2 million tonnes to 59.7 million, while wheat was down 1.4 million at 69.4 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Estimated cereals outputs for 1996 were 58.6 and 64.4 million tonnes respectively, the IGC said.</p>
<p>Most cereals sectors showed a reduction in the 1997 forecasts and the only one to see an improvement was maize -- expected to rise by 400,000 tonnes to 6.8 million tonnes.</p>
<p>--Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
